WEBVTT

00:06.140 --> 00:08.330
Please! I'm begging you!

00:09.230 --> 00:11.570
You're so persistent!

00:11.570 --> 00:13.320
You want money that badly?!

00:14.740 --> 00:18.570
You don't have to pay me back. 
Just never show your face in front of me again!

00:22.550 --> 00:23.910
I'll be borrowing this...

00:32.470 --> 00:36.690
Spice and Wolf

00:36.690 --> 00:37.810
Spice and Wolf

00:37.810 --> 00:43.150
Spice and Wolf

02:03.260 --> 02:08.100
<b>Episode 10
Wisdom of a Wolf and
Smooth Talk of a Merchant</b>

02:08.530 --> 02:10.510
Looks like you're back early.

02:27.010 --> 02:28.040
Holo.

02:36.180 --> 02:37.130
I'm sorry.

02:50.700 --> 02:53.150
This was what I was able to gather on my own.

02:54.730 --> 03:00.450
I still need over forty Lumione, 
but I'm out of options.

03:00.990 --> 03:04.410
The only other thing I can think of 
is trying my luck at the gambling house.

03:04.690 --> 03:10.030
I believe that money can grow 
exponentially when it's in the right hands.

03:10.030 --> 03:12.920
That's why I want you to hold on to this money.

03:13.460 --> 03:18.850
And, if we're bound to fail anyways, 
we might as well spend everything we have.

03:19.390 --> 03:24.050
Nothing will change 
even if I fall further into debt.

03:31.500 --> 03:34.820
Hey! I'm about to lock up!

03:52.740 --> 03:53.980
Fool!

03:53.980 --> 03:55.630
Come back up quickly!

04:01.300 --> 04:02.840
Uh...

04:04.510 --> 04:07.430
My companion threw out 
my purse from the window.

04:07.430 --> 04:09.590
Give me a break.

04:13.630 --> 04:14.650
You fool!

04:15.140 --> 04:16.150
I'm sorry.

04:17.070 --> 04:17.980
The money...

04:18.980 --> 04:20.890
How did you manage to collect it?

04:20.890 --> 04:21.980
You want to know?

04:24.220 --> 04:28.420
What would you have done 
if I ran away with your precious money?

04:28.420 --> 04:31.060
I collected the money with that half in mind.

04:31.940 --> 04:35.780
If my mistake prevents me 
from keeping my promise,

04:36.210 --> 04:38.630
I wanted to at least provide 
some traveling funds...

04:40.670 --> 04:43.670
You wished to leave me traveling funds?!

04:43.670 --> 04:45.550
Y-Yeah.

04:45.550 --> 04:49.220
How dare you spout such stupidity!

04:50.900 --> 04:52.680
I am the one at fault!

04:53.170 --> 04:55.930
You would have been able to 
borrow money if I were absent!

04:55.930 --> 04:58.110
Why are you not angrier?!

04:58.110 --> 04:59.540
I...

04:59.540 --> 05:00.920
I...

05:00.920 --> 05:02.990
I was the one in the wrong.

05:02.990 --> 05:05.530
You came along because 
you were worried about me.

05:05.860 --> 05:08.070
How could I be angry at—

05:08.950 --> 05:11.910
You fool!

05:16.740 --> 05:17.330
You!

05:18.500 --> 05:19.130
Watch out!

05:41.950 --> 05:43.110
You...

05:46.650 --> 05:48.240
You are too good-natured...

05:49.140 --> 05:50.970
Good-natured?

05:50.970 --> 05:52.330
Am I not right?!

05:52.940 --> 05:57.460
You were unable to borrow money 
because I went with you...

05:58.140 --> 06:00.000
Even so... Even so...

06:00.000 --> 06:02.310
I swatted your hand away.

06:02.750 --> 06:04.700
That was wrong of me.

06:04.700 --> 06:08.380
I forced you to take me along 
due to my selfishness.

06:08.380 --> 06:11.640
Since my actions backfired on you, 
you should be angrier at me!

06:14.050 --> 06:17.890
On top of that, if you apologize 
to me in such a way, I...

06:18.250 --> 06:19.290
I...

06:19.890 --> 06:20.890
I'm sorry.

06:21.490 --> 06:27.490
I really thought I did something I couldn't 
take back when I swatted your hand away.

06:28.030 --> 06:31.410
I really wanted to apologize 
over and over for that.

06:32.030 --> 06:35.660
That's why I thought 
I should do the best I could.

06:35.960 --> 06:40.070
My actions seemed to have backfired. I'm sorry.

06:43.820 --> 06:44.800
You...

06:46.270 --> 06:48.750
Answer me this.

06:49.210 --> 06:54.970
Wh-Why are you this good-natured?

07:03.870 --> 07:05.650
It's probably my personality.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.530
Y-You!

07:09.340 --> 07:11.260
I cannot believe this!

07:11.260 --> 07:13.200
You are unbelievably good-natured!

07:13.540 --> 07:14.870
You fool!

07:17.250 --> 07:19.580
P-Personality?

07:19.580 --> 07:21.040
Your personality?!

07:21.360 --> 07:24.200
Even if it is a lie, an astute male should say

07:24.200 --> 07:27.720
their actions are a sign 
of their affection! You fool!

07:27.720 --> 07:29.140
S-Sorry.

07:29.140 --> 07:30.500
Actually, the truth is...

07:30.500 --> 07:32.930
Now, listen here.

07:33.850 --> 07:36.650
There are times when one wishes 
to hear something even if it is a lie

07:36.650 --> 07:39.040
and times when one wishes to beat the other

07:39.040 --> 07:41.560
until their face is swollen because 
it is spoken too late.

07:42.130 --> 07:44.440
Which time do you think it is now?

07:45.370 --> 07:46.320
The latter...

07:46.320 --> 07:49.110
Your good nature is unparalleled!

07:49.440 --> 07:53.570
Just how many males in the world 
would refrain from saying

07:53.570 --> 07:57.510
they love or value a female in such 
a situation to woo her with ease?

07:57.510 --> 08:01.290
Though, it is easy to read 
your thoughts on the matter.

08:02.730 --> 08:09.170
And, well, I am able to travel with a light 
heart because of your good nature.

08:09.170 --> 08:13.130
It may be too lavish to wish for everything.

08:16.220 --> 08:19.620
Even so, I wished to hear those words.

08:20.450 --> 08:22.310
So, let us try again.

08:23.220 --> 08:26.530
Why are you so good-natured?

08:29.610 --> 08:31.780
Because you're special to me.

09:07.740 --> 09:10.820
Goodness. What in the world are we doing?

09:10.820 --> 09:13.030
You're the one who made us do it!

09:14.510 --> 09:17.740
Well, was it not good practice for you?

09:18.040 --> 09:19.370
Goodness...

09:19.370 --> 09:21.130
But you know...

09:22.020 --> 09:24.620
Next time, you should make me upset.

09:24.620 --> 09:27.620
I am happy about your consideration,

09:27.620 --> 09:32.890
but problems may oft be resolved faster 
if we grow angry and argue with one another.

09:32.890 --> 09:33.710
All right.

09:34.940 --> 09:38.840
You were right to have 
grand expectations of my wisdom.

09:38.840 --> 09:42.310
After all, I have a good idea in mind.

09:42.310 --> 09:43.090
Wha?!

09:43.710 --> 09:44.510
What is it?!

09:55.310 --> 09:56.900
Please wait here.

10:03.660 --> 10:05.890
I'm here by your side.

10:09.790 --> 10:10.580
Yeah.

10:17.830 --> 10:20.450
I heard you have some 
important business with me?

10:21.670 --> 10:24.580
Smuggling gold?! You can't be serious.

10:24.580 --> 10:25.970
I'm completely serious.

10:29.040 --> 10:35.030
People who are at the brink of bankruptcy 
often confuse a reckless plan as a perfect one.

10:35.030 --> 10:38.570
What if the gold is smuggled 
by an extremely skilled person?

10:39.770 --> 10:43.280
Your plan is impossible to put into motion.

10:43.280 --> 10:48.560
If such a skilled person existed, they would be 
making plenty of money on their own.

10:48.560 --> 10:52.460
What if the extremely skilled person 
isn't making good money?

10:52.730 --> 10:56.740
If they're that skilled, they shouldn't 
have problems finding work in this city.

10:56.740 --> 11:00.630
What if they are skilled, 
earning low wages in this city,

11:00.630 --> 11:04.300
and are in desperate need of money?

11:04.720 --> 11:09.820
Most importantly, the individual is 
frustrated with their current employer...

11:09.820 --> 11:13.610
and the employer of that person is the Church.

11:13.610 --> 11:17.360
If I convince her that smuggling gold 
would be an act against the Church,

11:17.360 --> 11:19.400
she will definitely accept the job.

11:19.400 --> 11:21.490
There is no chance of betrayal.

11:21.490 --> 11:25.760
Th-Then, why not smuggle 
the gold with just yourselves?

11:25.760 --> 11:28.290
There's no reason to come to me!

11:28.290 --> 11:30.080
I have two reasons.

11:30.080 --> 11:35.110
First, the deadline 
for my debt with you is today.

11:35.830 --> 11:37.310
Second...

11:39.590 --> 11:43.180
this is all the money I currently have.

11:45.470 --> 11:47.800
I was only able to collect 
three and two-sevenths Lumione

11:47.800 --> 11:50.210
after running around all day.

11:50.210 --> 11:52.280
This is everything I have.

11:52.280 --> 11:55.200
I would like to use this 
as collateral for this proposal.

11:55.200 --> 11:59.020
With it, I would like you to hold off 
on collecting the debt

11:59.020 --> 12:02.280
and provide enough money 
for the purchase of the gold.

12:02.580 --> 12:03.410
Wha?!

12:06.980 --> 12:08.180
Great sir.

12:08.830 --> 12:10.950
Do you have the time to hesitate?

12:11.810 --> 12:15.460
It seems yet another person has left just now.

12:15.460 --> 12:17.570
Is it all right to drag your feet?

12:18.630 --> 12:23.410
Since my ears are especially good, 
I can easily hear their whispering.

12:23.410 --> 12:27.290
In the room below us, there are people 
planning to abandon you and run away.

12:27.290 --> 12:29.310
Should I repeat their words in detail?

12:31.820 --> 12:35.440
I see. The crash of the armor market has 
brought this trading company tremendous losses.

12:35.960 --> 12:42.460
They're saying, "Let's run. This place has 
no future. Let's gather the others together."

12:42.890 --> 12:44.530
At this rate, this company...

12:44.530 --> 12:45.830
Stop it!

12:50.090 --> 12:52.290
What do you think, Mr. Remerio?

12:52.620 --> 12:58.370
If you wait for me to pay you back 
and I get a reasonable cut from this deal...

12:58.710 --> 13:02.550
I'm sure it's not a bad deal for you as well.

13:03.230 --> 13:05.980
What do you think, Mr. Remerio?

13:18.850 --> 13:20.230
I'll do it.

13:24.990 --> 13:27.250
May God overlook our actions...

13:36.620 --> 13:38.380
Call Liebert here.

13:39.020 --> 13:43.340
I am surprised he had enough funds to buy gold.

13:43.340 --> 13:46.560
Most trading companies put aside 
fiercely protected emergency funds

13:46.560 --> 13:49.340
to recover from drastic and unexpected losses.

13:49.660 --> 13:51.800
I wanted to dip into those funds.

13:51.800 --> 13:53.310
I see.

13:53.310 --> 13:54.500
Now, then.

13:55.230 --> 13:57.560
How confident are you in conning a young woman?

13:57.560 --> 13:59.610
Don't put it like that.

13:59.610 --> 14:01.170
Am I wrong?

14:01.620 --> 14:02.940
Well, you're not.

14:02.940 --> 14:05.410
You are too good-natured.

14:05.410 --> 14:11.210
But, well, I am able to travel with a light 
heart because of your good nature.

14:11.910 --> 14:14.950
I can go in your place and cajole her.

14:15.380 --> 14:18.000
I need to make myself a little useful.

14:18.250 --> 14:20.300
Are you still bothered by yesterday?

14:20.300 --> 14:21.500
Not really...

14:21.500 --> 14:26.420
Who knows what would have happened 
if you didn't corner Remerio just now.

14:26.840 --> 14:28.940
You've been plenty useful.

14:28.940 --> 14:30.100
Is that so?

14:31.540 --> 14:37.100
I'm the one who was blinded by greed on an item 
that had already crashed in the markets.

14:37.440 --> 14:39.390
I'll convince her myself.

14:40.350 --> 14:44.050
And, if I get your help for every little thing,

14:44.050 --> 14:46.780
who knows how much advantage 
you'll take of me later.

14:49.270 --> 14:50.490
How unfortunate.

14:50.490 --> 14:54.800
I was hoping to get you deep into debt 
with me so I could collect more later.

14:54.800 --> 14:56.080
That was a close one.

14:56.080 --> 14:58.180
I almost fell for it.

15:07.070 --> 15:08.220
Hello!

15:08.220 --> 15:08.860
Huh?

15:09.970 --> 15:11.130
Oh...

15:11.890 --> 15:14.650
Mr. Lawrence and Ms. Holo?

15:14.650 --> 15:16.860
I can't believe we ran into you 
in front of the church!

15:16.860 --> 15:18.680
God must have brought us together!

15:18.680 --> 15:21.290
Even I wouldn't be fooled by such words.

15:21.290 --> 15:22.350
That's good to hear.

15:22.740 --> 15:26.690
I heard there were people who drink 
too much holy blood during church, so... {Note: In other words, drank too much wine and get drunk.}

15:27.010 --> 15:30.480
I can't drink much, 
so I rarely touch wine myself.

15:30.480 --> 15:31.360
So, um...

15:31.360 --> 15:33.320
Actually, I'd like to offer you a job.

15:33.320 --> 15:34.810
Really?!

15:39.080 --> 15:41.060
We should discuss this elsewhere.

15:41.910 --> 15:42.930
Yes.

15:44.660 --> 15:46.110
Cheers to our reunion!

15:54.340 --> 15:58.050
So, didn't you say you could go 
as far as Lamtra, Ms. Nora?

15:58.050 --> 16:00.360
Y-Yes, I can.

16:00.360 --> 16:02.300
Even while herding sheep?

16:02.300 --> 16:04.270
As long as there aren't too many...

16:07.380 --> 16:12.240
There is a job I'd like to hire you for. 
The pay is twenty Lumione.

16:12.500 --> 16:14.690
T-Twenty?!

16:14.690 --> 16:16.990
But that amount is only if we succeed.

16:17.340 --> 16:20.330
It's a dangerous job, 
so there will be no pay if we fail.

16:23.810 --> 16:28.830
Your job is to take your sheep there 
and to come back safely with them.

16:29.810 --> 16:33.320
Your herding skills as a shepherd 
are all that is required.

16:33.320 --> 16:34.800
Then, why...

16:34.800 --> 16:35.430
But!

16:35.870 --> 16:37.720
But it will be extremely dangerous.

16:37.720 --> 16:40.420
Dangerous enough to fit the pay.

16:40.720 --> 16:44.870
At most, the fee to join the tailor 
association would be one Lumione.

16:45.260 --> 16:46.170
If you have twenty Lumione,

16:46.170 --> 16:49.110
you'll be able to work without worrying 
about any immediate living expenses.

16:50.460 --> 16:53.860
In fact, you may even be able to buy 
your way into a master tailor position.

16:54.140 --> 16:57.570
Then, you'll become the owner 
of Nora's Clothing Store.

17:03.700 --> 17:05.160
Oh, that's right.

17:05.160 --> 17:08.690
Were you planning on joining 
the association here?

17:08.690 --> 17:12.440
N-No, I was planning on 
registering in a different town.

17:12.440 --> 17:13.670
I see.

17:14.010 --> 17:17.610
Since this city is so big, 
wouldn't it be better to register here?

17:17.610 --> 17:21.350
It'll be hard to live in a new town 
where no one knows who you are.

17:24.430 --> 17:29.650
Well, I'm sure you don't want to be 
involved with the Church in this city.

17:29.650 --> 17:34.440
Th-That's not really true...

17:34.440 --> 17:41.740
The harder you work and do your best 
to protect their valuable sheep,

17:41.740 --> 17:45.870
the more they suspect you to be 
a heretic with diabolic powers.

17:45.870 --> 17:47.060
Am I wrong?

17:48.500 --> 17:52.380
They keep trying to reveal your true colors

17:52.380 --> 17:56.670
by sending you to dangerous areas 
other shepherds would never go to.

17:57.690 --> 18:01.660
I'm sure the priest here will keep 
sending you to dangerous places

18:01.660 --> 18:05.550
until you are attacked 
by wolves or mercenaries.

18:05.550 --> 18:10.110
Every single day, they continue 
to suspect that you are a heretic.

18:10.500 --> 18:12.750
I've also had a similar experience.

18:13.220 --> 18:14.400
Let me be straight with you.

18:15.650 --> 18:17.820
The Church here is worse than pigs.

18:19.130 --> 18:22.200
So, we've made a plan.

18:25.410 --> 18:28.240
You'll cause a little trouble for 
the Church, earn some money,

18:28.240 --> 18:29.580
and go to a different town.

18:29.940 --> 18:31.290
That's the kind of plan this is.

18:37.110 --> 18:38.380
We'll smuggle gold.

18:42.350 --> 18:45.930
But, what use am I to you?

18:48.390 --> 18:54.880
As you know, this city is very strict 
on the smuggling of gold.

18:54.880 --> 18:55.780
Yes...

18:56.060 --> 19:00.290
We plan to hide the gold 
under the bellies of the sheep

19:00.290 --> 19:03.780
and secretly bring in a large amount 
of gold without being caught.

19:05.530 --> 19:06.620
I see.

19:06.620 --> 19:12.540
However, the price of gold is exorbitant 
in any of the towns influenced by this city.

19:12.540 --> 19:14.880
But there's one exception.

19:15.250 --> 19:17.510
The pagan town, Lamtra.

19:17.920 --> 19:21.090
Many people travel the safe route to Lamtra,

19:21.090 --> 19:25.260
and it's been the territory of 
other shepherds for a long time.

19:25.560 --> 19:28.220
That's why I chose you, Ms. Nora.

19:28.220 --> 19:32.800
No one will suspect you for traveling 
through secluded areas with your sheep.

19:32.800 --> 19:36.980
On top of that, you'll be taking 
the shortest route to Lamtra.

19:36.980 --> 19:43.350
Also, for you, this is the perfect chance 
to get back at the Church.

19:43.620 --> 19:46.600
The import and export of gold, 
along with donations,

19:46.600 --> 19:48.370
are the greatest sources 
of income for the Church.

19:48.370 --> 19:52.040
However, if they discover us, 
we will be severely punished.

19:52.040 --> 19:56.090
After we finish this job, we'll have to 
leave this city to ensure our safety.

19:56.610 --> 19:59.870
But the reward will be twenty Lumione.

20:13.190 --> 20:15.310
Please allow me to take this job.

20:26.010 --> 20:27.570
I look forward to working with you.

20:28.330 --> 20:29.460
I, as well.

20:33.080 --> 20:35.580
Then, let's talk in more detail.

20:36.580 --> 20:39.590
Hey, why are you not happier?

20:39.920 --> 20:42.010
Things have gone well.

20:42.830 --> 20:48.000
No matter what profits are involved, 
it's never enough to gamble your life.

20:48.000 --> 20:49.640
Well, that is true.

20:49.640 --> 20:54.100
And I only talked about the profits 
involved. It's practically fraud!

20:54.590 --> 20:58.800
It's normal to call a merchant who signs
 an unfavorable contract with another a fool.

20:58.800 --> 20:59.820
But she's not a merchant.

21:00.420 --> 21:02.220
She's just a young shepherd!

21:03.950 --> 21:07.200
You are truly hopelessly good-natured.

21:07.570 --> 21:11.870
That girl is not a mere sheep 
to be hunted as prey and eaten.

21:12.340 --> 21:17.960
She is a daring sheep that decided to 
jump into a circle of wild animals herself.

21:17.960 --> 21:22.370
She may be a different animal 
wearing a sheep's skin.

21:23.840 --> 21:28.150
I do not wish to say this, 
but she is a talented shepherd.

21:28.540 --> 21:31.690
Well, you are not too bad yourself.

21:32.180 --> 21:33.290
I see.

21:33.290 --> 21:36.690
Although, you are also not one 
to be underestimated.

21:36.940 --> 21:38.170
Of course.

21:38.170 --> 21:40.480
Be careful not to be seduced by my charm.

21:42.340 --> 21:43.740
I will wait with anticipation.

21:43.740 --> 21:47.860
Well, we'll have to work hard to make sure 
we can all laugh at the end of this.

21:47.860 --> 21:49.460
A reasonable way of thinking.

21:49.460 --> 21:50.420
However...

21:52.080 --> 21:56.160
I think that the two of us chuckling 
together alone is the most appealing.

21:59.650 --> 22:03.960
An attractive idea, but I still wish 
for everyone to laugh together.

22:06.010 --> 22:09.080
You are just too good-natured.

22:09.080 --> 22:09.890
No good?

22:09.890 --> 22:11.130
Do not be silly.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 11

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Forest of Wolves and Frigid Rain

23:45.860 --> 23:49.670
Next Episode: "Forest of Wolves and Frigid Rain".
